course: dictionary
lesson: 15228
title: Sewn: joined with a needle and thread
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Sewn is a form of the verb sew, which means to join things with a needle and thread. Use sewn when the sewing is already finished. «My name is sewn into my coat.» The name was sewn in earlier, and now it is there.
explain: Look for clues around the word. Needles, thread, cloth, buttons and patches all point to sewing. In «The patch was sewn on my jeans», the patch is fixed on with thread, so sewn means joined that way.
explain: Sewn also appears in sport talk. «The match is sewn up.» Here sewn up is informal, and nobody is sewing anything. Ask: what word would fit? Certain fits, so the match is settled and the win is sure.
fact: Sewn is a form of the verb sew: sew, sews, sewed, sewn or sewed, sewing.
fact: «Sewn» means joined or fixed with a needle and thread.
fact: «Sewn up» is informal and means settled or certain to be won.
fact: Phrases to know: sewn on, sewn up, hand-sewn.
fact: A good check is to swap in "fixed with thread". If it still makes sense in the sentence, you have the right meaning.
exercise: «The badge was sewn onto my school bag.» What does sewn mean here? | *Fixed on with a needle and thread | Lost under the bed | Painted in bright colours | Drawn with a pencil
exercise: «The team scored twice, so the match is sewn up.» What does sewn up mean here? | Torn into pieces | Started late | *Certain to be won | Hidden in a box
exercise: Mum says the hem of the skirt was hand-sewn. What does hand-sewn mean? | Painted by hand | Shaped like a hand | *Joined by hand with a needle and thread | Made by a machine
test: I have ___ a name tag onto my PE bag. Which word fits? | sew | sews | *sewn | sewing
test: «Our team is so far ahead that the cup is sewn up.» What does sewn up mean? | Lost and forgotten | Covered in wool | Torn at the seams | *Certain to be won
exam: Which phrase in the lesson means the win is certain? | *sewn up | needle and thread | hand-sewn | sewn on
